<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saarland</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Saarland is a state of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and Luxembourg, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saarbrucken">Saarbrücken</a>. Formed as the Territory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saar-river">Saar</a> Basin under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> administration in 1920, it voted to return to Germany in 1935, came under French control after 1945 and joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a> in 1957 after a referendum. Its economy long rested on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saarland.jpg" alt="Saarland" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Saarland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
